WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:05.133
When I married, I moved out of the Baker Street rooms that I shared with Sherlock Holmes.

2
00:00:05.134 --> 00:00:11.306
At first the great detective continued to call upon me when he needed someone to accompany him on his investigations.

3
00:00:11.307 --> 00:00:15.168
But as the years passed, those occasions became less frequent.

4
00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:20.701
I’d recently read in the newspapers that Holmes was working on an important matter for the French government.

5
00:00:20.768 --> 00:00:25.628
So you can imagine my surprise when he suddenly appeared in my study one April evening.

6
00:00:25.629 --> 00:00:29.359
I immediately noticed that he looked quite pale and thin.

7
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.953
“Yes, Dr. Watson, your observations are correct,” he said in response to my concerned glance.

8
00:00:34.954 --> 00:00:39.957
“I’ve been under some strain lately. Do you mind if I close the shutters over your window?”

9
00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:45.045
Before I could reply, he edged around the room and bolted the shutters securely.

10
00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:49.366
The only light in the room came from a lamp near the chair where I had been reading.

11
00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:52.434
“You’re afraid of something?” I asked.

12
00:00:52.435 --> 00:00:54.932
“An air gun,” he replied.

13
00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:58.117
“My dear Holmes, what are you talking about?”

14
00:00:58.118 --> 00:01:02.113
“I think you know me well enough, Watson, to understand that I’m not a nervous man.”

15
00:01:02.114 --> 00:01:03.922
Holmes stepped closer.

16
00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:08.164
“However, I would be stupid to refuse to recognize danger when it’s nearby.”

17
00:01:08.376 --> 00:01:12.285
Holmes held out his hand, and I saw that two knuckles were bleeding.

18
00:01:12.286 --> 00:01:15.024
“You’ve been in a fight!” I cried.

19
00:01:15.025 --> 00:01:18.652
“Yes, I’m involved in something quite serious.”

20
00:01:18.653 --> 00:01:24.316
Holmes’ eyes shone with the familiar excitement that meant he was deeply absorbed in a case.

21
00:01:25.072 --> 00:01:27.023
“Is Mrs. Watson at home?”

22
00:01:27.024 --> 00:01:30.330
“No, she’s away for a few days visiting a relative.”

23
00:01:30.331 --> 00:01:34.404
“Good! Then it’s easier for me to propose that you join me for a week away.”

24
00:01:34.405 --> 00:01:36.086
“Where are we going?”

25
00:01:36.087 --> 00:01:39.565
“Oh, anywhere. It’s all the same to me.”

26
00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:44.991
“This is very strange,” I thought as I fetched a basin of water and a cloth for his hand.

27
00:01:44.992 --> 00:01:51.735
It wasn’t like Holmes to take aimless vacations, and something about his face suggested that his nerves were at the breaking point.

28
00:01:51.736 --> 00:01:55.412
After Holmes cleaned up his injury, he took a seat facing me.

29
00:01:55.413 --> 00:01:57.937
“Have you ever heard of Professor Moriarty?”

30
00:01:57.938 --> 00:02:03.467
Holmes leaned forward, putting his fingertips together and resting his elbows on his knees.

31
00:02:03.468 --> 00:02:05.356
I shook my head.

32
00:02:06.046 --> 00:02:07.769
“You’re not alone, Watson.

33
00:02:08.018 --> 00:02:12.357
He’s one of the most influential men in London, and yet no one has heard of him.

34
00:02:12.636 --> 00:02:17.294
If I could free society from that man, it would be the peak of my career.

35
00:02:17.295 --> 00:02:20.707
Then I could retire to a quieter line of work.”

36
00:02:20.708 --> 00:02:22.582
“What has he done?”

37
00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:30.551
Holmes told me that Moriarty had been an unusually brilliant, prize-winning mathematics professor at a small university outside London.

38
00:02:30.552 --> 00:02:36.373
However, when rumors of criminal activity swirled around him, he had to resign his position.

39
00:02:36.374 --> 00:02:41.693
“As you are aware, Watson, no one knows the London criminal world as well as I do.

40
00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:47.966
For years I’ve been conscious of a link between all sorts of cases—forgeries, robberies, murders.

41
00:02:48.071 --> 00:02:51.874
But I could never figure out what the link was until now.”

42
00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:57.316
Holmes explained that Moriarty was the mastermind behind the worst crimes in the city.

43
00:02:57.317 --> 00:03:00.776
“The professor never actually participates in the crimes.

44
00:03:00.777 --> 00:03:06.424
Instead he commands a whole network of people who carry out his diabolical plans.

45
00:03:06.425 --> 00:03:10.448
He’s like the spider that waits quietly in the center of the web.”

46
00:03:10.449 --> 00:03:13.569
“What happens when his people get caught?” I asked.

47
00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:17.801
“Don’t they tell the police about Moriarty in an attempt to save themselves?”

48
00:03:17.802 --> 00:03:22.325
“Whenever someone is caught, money quickly appears for bail or a lawyer.

49
00:03:22.326 --> 00:03:25.837
No one ever suspects Moriarty is behind it all.”

50
00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.888
Holmes had pursued the professor for three months.

51
00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:34.174
Every time he had been about to close in on Moriarty, the genius managed to escape.

52
00:03:34.175 --> 00:03:38.347
Holmes was forced to admit that he had met his intellectual equal.

53
00:03:39.632 --> 00:03:43.216
But recently Moriarty had made a tiny mistake.

54
00:03:43.217 --> 00:03:51.710
Holmes did not explain what that was, saying only that on Monday, three days from now, the professor and his main gang members would be arrested.

55
00:03:51.711 --> 00:03:58.075
“There’s enough evidence to convict them of more than forty crimes,” Holmes said with a look of satisfaction.

56
00:03:58.076 --> 00:04:01.117
“It’ll be the criminal trial of the century.”

57
00:04:01.118 --> 00:04:04.463
“Don’t you want to be around to see that?” I asked.

58
00:04:04.464 --> 00:04:07.435
“Are you sure you want to leave London?”

59
00:04:07.436 --> 00:04:11.466
“That’s a recent decision—made early this morning, as a matter of fact.”

60
00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:15.005
Holmes gave me a bitter laugh.

61
00:04:15.006 --> 00:04:21.943
“I was sitting in my study in my dressing gown, thinking over the case, when the door opened and Professor Moriarty stood before me.”

62
00:04:21.943 --> 00:04:25.671
I gasped and Holmes said he’d been surprised too.

63
00:04:26.172 --> 00:04:31.059
“I was familiar with the professor’s appearance, but it was startling to see him in the flesh.”

64
00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:37.629
Holmes explained that Moriarty was extremely tall and thin with sunken eyes and a clean-shaven face.

65
00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.022
He had peered at Holmes with great curiosity.

66
00:04:41.023 --> 00:04:48.192
“Moriarty smiled,” Holmes went on, “but there was something in his eyes that made me wish that I had my revolver close by.”

67
00:04:48.193 --> 00:04:51.989
I found the rest of Holmes’ story fascinating and frightening.

68
00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:55.097
Holmes had beckoned for Moriarty to take a seat.

69
00:04:55.098 --> 00:04:59.111
“If you have anything to say, Professor, I can spare you five minutes.”

70
00:04:59.112 --> 00:05:04.890
As Moriarty sat down, he reached into his pocket, and Holmes feared that he was reaching for a gun.

71
00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:09.650
But Moriarty pulled out a notebook in which he’d scribbled some dates.

72
00:05:09.991 --> 00:05:14.847
“You crossed my path on January 4,” Moriarty read aloud.

73
00:05:14.848 --> 00:05:17.578
“On January 23 you bothered me.

74
00:05:17.579 --> 00:05:21.781
By the middle of February, I was seriously inconvenienced by you.

75
00:05:21.782 --> 00:05:30.112
At the end of March, you ruined my plans, and now in April, I find that I am in danger of losing my liberty, thanks to you.

76
00:05:30.113 --> 00:05:34.444
This situation has become impossible. You must give up.”

77
00:05:34.445 --> 00:05:37.176
“After Monday,” Holmes said.

78
00:05:37.177 --> 00:05:43.228
“It’s been an intellectual treat for me to see how you’ve grappled with this affair,” Moriarty said.

79
00:05:43.229 --> 00:05:47.947
“A man with your brain should be able to see that there can be only one outcome.

80
00:05:47.948 --> 00:05:52.387
It would distress me to have to take an extreme measure against you.”

81
00:05:52.388 --> 00:05:54.947
Holmes was unbothered by the threat.

82
00:05:54.948 --> 00:05:59.776
“I long ago accepted that danger is a part of my profession.”

83
00:05:59.777 --> 00:06:03.008
“This is not danger!” Moriarty snapped.

84
00:06:03.009 --> 00:06:05.213
“It’s inevitable destruction.

85
00:06:05.214 --> 00:06:13.276
You stand in the way not merely of an individual but also of a mighty organization, the full extent of which you cannot comprehend.”

86
00:06:13.277 --> 00:06:19.302
Holmes stood up. “This has been a pleasant conversation, but I’m neglecting important business elsewhere.”

87
00:06:19.303 --> 00:06:23.431
Shaking his head sadly, Moriarty looked at Holmes in silence.

88
00:06:23.432 --> 00:06:26.806
“Well, it’s a pity,” the professor said at last.

89
00:06:26.807 --> 00:06:29.309
“I’ve done what I could to warn you.

90
00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:34.336
Even if you’re clever enough to kill me, rest assured that one of my men will do the same to you.

91
00:06:34.337 --> 00:06:36.923
He already has my instructions.”

